    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "p2p: select another peer after empty headers",
    "user": {
      "login": "l0rinc",
      "id": 1841944,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDE5NDQ=",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1841944?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/l0rinc",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "**Problem:** During IBD, the node asks one peer at a time for the headers needed to catch up.\r\nThat peer can send valid empty `headers`, which the node accepts while still treating the peer as active, so no replacement is selected.\r\nWhen all peers are inbound, the headers timeout cannot release that peer either.\r\n\r\n**Fix:** Stop treating the peer as active after an empty response while the best header is at least a day old, and clear its headers timeout.\r\nKeep the time of the recent `getheaders` request so the same peer is not selected again immediately, while a later block announcement can still retry it.\r\nIf an outbound peer is already waiting to be disconnected because its chain is old, keep that check running after another peer takes over headers sync.\r\n\r\n<details><summary>Manual reproducer</summary>\r\n\r\nBoth runs use the checked-out `build/bin/bitcoind`; [Python](https://gist.github.com/l0rinc/39e471dd6835fe332205d3812ebb9e92) only supplies two inbound P2P peers.\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nDATADIR=\"$(mktemp -d /tmp/bitcoin-empty-headers.XXXXXX)\"\r\ntrap 'build/bin/bitcoin-cli -regtest -datadir=\"$DATADIR\" -rpcport=18454 stop >/dev/null 2>&1; rm -rf \"$DATADIR\"' EXIT\r\n\r\n{ cmake -B build && cmake --build build -j --target bitcoind bitcoin-cli; } >/dev/null 2>&1\r\nbuild/bin/bitcoind -regtest -daemonwait -datadir=\"$DATADIR\" -connect=0 -listen=1 -port=18455 -rpcport=18454\r\ntime python3 '/Users/lorinc/Library/Application Support/JetBrains/CLion2026.1/scratches/scratch_758.py'\r\nkillall bitcoind\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe fixed node returns as soon as the replacement peer receives `getheaders`.\r\nOn the old node, that wait times out after 10 seconds because the initial peer is still treated as active.\r\n</details>\r\n",
